 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Nagiyev tastes the dish, and he is amazed. He can't believe the little cook did it. The Russian comes first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это божественно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это очень вкусно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я не ожидал такого.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Повезло тебе, поварёнок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Дмитрий Владимирович.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ну, всем повезло.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Наш ресторан лучший.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Гости очень довольны.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мы сделали это.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Теперь можно отдыхать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Отличная работа, команда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Браво!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "The tasting, line by line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это божественно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is divine.' 'Bozhestvenno' comes from 'bog', god. It's a very strong compliment, and English uses 'divine' the same way.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это очень вкусно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is very tasty.' 'Tasty' needs no 'is', and 'very' goes in front. It's the shortest praise in the language.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я не ожидал такого.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I didn't expect this.' 'Expected' ends in a bare consonant for a man. 'Such' takes an 'o' ending to show it's the thing not expected.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Повезло тебе, поварёнок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You are lucky, little chef.' 'Povezlo tebe' is 'it was lucky to you', so luck is a thing that happens to you. 'Povaryonok' is a nickname, 'little cook'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Дмитрий Владимирович.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Dmitry Vladimirovich.' First name plus father's name is the respectful way to address a boss. Max says it to thank him, very carefully.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ну, всем повезло.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, we're all lucky.' 'Vsem povezlo' is 'to all it was lucky', the same luck pattern as before. 'Vsem' is 'to everyone'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Наш ресторан лучший.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Our restaurant is the best.' 'Luchshiy' means 'the best', and there's no 'is'. Nagiyev says it with satisfaction.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Гости очень довольны.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The guests are very pleased.' 'Pleased' is a plural here, to match 'guests'. It's a short form with no extra word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мы сделали это.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We did it.' 'My sdelali eto' is 'we did this', and Russians like to say 'we' about team victories.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Теперь можно отдыхать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Now we can rest.' 'Mozhno' means 'we may', 'it's allowed', and 'otdykhat' is 'to rest'. 'Teper' is 'now'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Отличная работа, команда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Excellent work, team.' 'Team' is feminine, so 'excellent' has an 'aya'. A Russian team is a 'she'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Браво!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Bravo!' It's the same as in English, and Russians say it to applaud too. No translation needed. Here is the tasting, uncut.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
